{
	# Local dev tooling wants real HTTPS for internal-only hostnames that
	# Let's Encrypt can never issue for. This mints certs from Caddy's own
	# built-in CA instead — trust it once with `caddy trust`.
	local_certs
}

# Site blocks with real hostnames/IPs are machine-local, never tracked here.
# `import Caddyfile.local` resolves relative to this file, not the process's
# CWD, so it always finds the sibling file below regardless of who starts
# caddy or from where. See create_private_dot_config/caddy/Caddyfile.local
# for the template and README's Caddy section for the full setup.
import Caddyfile.local
